-- title:
--   Node order bound by branch orders of the two reductions
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, a nonzero level $N$, an algebraically closed perfect field $k$ of characteristic $q$, a ring homomorphism $red : A \to k$, modular polynomial data for $q$ satisfying the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \equiv (X'^q - X)(X' - X^q)$ mod $q$, integrality of the two Hecke maps $\bar\alpha,\bar\beta$ from level $N$ to level $Nq$, a place specialization $P$ and a prolongation tuple $R$ for $P$. Assume $q \nmid N$, that $R$ is a model (the two divisor laws and the two cusp laws), that $R$ satisfies the order law at Frobenius-fixed affine places, and that for a finite set $W_0$ of supersingular places of `modularFunctionFieldC k N` (each rational, affine and with supersingular $j$-value) the regularity and node-value laws hold. Let $K \le K'$ be intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q}$ with $K'$ finite over $\mathbb{Q}$, and $w \in W_0$ with $\mathrm{Frob}\cdot w \in W_0$, such that the value-integrality law holds at $w$ and the node ring over $K$ at $w$ is contained in that over $K'$. Let $\varpi \in A \cap K'$ generate the kernel of the reduction on $A \cap K'$ (i.e. $red\,d = 0$ iff $\varpi \mid d$), and $q = \varpi^{e_{K}}\varepsilon$ with $e_K \ge 1$ and $\varepsilon$ a unit. Let $c$ be node coordinates $(x,y)$ over $K$ at $w$ (first residue of $x$ zero, $\mathrm{ord}_{\mathrm{Frob}\cdot w}$ of the second residue of $x$ equal to $1$, second residue of $y$ zero, $\mathrm{ord}_w$ of its first residue equal to $1$), with an exact node equation $xy = \varpi^{e_w e_K}u$ in the node ring over $K'$ at $w$ for some $e_w \ge 1$ and unit $u$, such that the ideal generated by $\varpi, x, y$ in that ring is maximal and is its only maximal ideal and equals its maximal ideal, the ring being local and noetherian; the two branch ideals $(\varpi,x)$ and $(\varpi,y)$ are prime with $y \notin (\varpi,x)$ and $x \notin (\varpi,y)$; and every element of the node ring becomes a non-unit after subtracting a suitable constant from $A \cap K'$. Let $\mathrm{depth}$ be a natural-number weight on the places of `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` satisfying the depth-value law for $c$: for every place $V$ reducing to $w$ under $P$ and fixed by the inertia group of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, the $A$-valuation of the value of $y$ at $V$ is the $A$-valuation of $q$ raised to $\mathrm{depth}\,V$. Let $f \ne 0$ lie in `modularFunctionFieldBar (N * q)` with $q$-expansion in the $K'$-rational subfield, assume every element of that subfield is a quotient of two elements of the node ring over $K'$ at $w$ with nonzero denominator, and let $c_1, c_2 \in K'$ be nonzero with $c_1 f$ integral for the first prolongation and of nonzero first residue, $c_2 f$ integral for the second prolongation and of nonzero second residue. Finally let $D$ be the divisor $D(V) = \mathrm{ord}_V f$ and assume every $V$ in its support with $P$-first reduction $w$ is fixed by the arithmetic Galois action of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Then $\sum_{V \in \mathrm{supp}\,D,\ P.\mathrm{reduceFst}\,V = w} D(V) \le \mathrm{ord}_w\bigl(R.\mathrm{residue}_1(c_1 f)\bigr) + \mathrm{ord}_{\mathrm{Frob}\cdot w}\bigl(R.\mathrm{residue}_2(c_2 f)\bigr)$, where $\mathrm{Frob} =$ `arithFrobC q k N`.
--
--   This is the one-sided (inequality) form of the local counting relation at a single supersingular node of the reduction of $X_0(Nq)$ at $q$: the total order of $\mathrm{div}(f)$ along the places lying over the node is bounded by the sum of the orders at the node of the two normalised one-sided reductions of $f$, computed through the crossing model $\widehat{W}[[U,V]]/(UV - \varpi^{e_we_K})$. It is used in the construction of component charts and annuli attached to a model, and in the component-group identity relating the depth pairing to the degree of the second reduction.
